I know, I know....another one....but hey, it's my first
ascension....I've been playing since there was no 'net' in 'Nethack',
and that damned imp was a major pain...I won't bore you with a step by
step account or the entire trip, but I will post the major plot
elements and lessons learned.





1) Altar in the first room I walked into on level one. My first sign I
was headed for a lucky game. I believe I had Mjollnir before I even
attempted the mines. Level 1 was my base of operations the entire game,
and I had about 7 chests and boxes in this room, filled with the things
I thought I would need for the planes. Incidentally, I would find about
3 more altars in the regular dungeons during the course of the game.

2) Mines.....No less than 4 bones piles encountered here (I use
Hearse), one of which contained a wand of wishing, magic lamp, bag of
holding, and a luckstone. I tamed the unfortunate soul's pet housecat,
Bast (name ring a bell for anyone?). There was no reason to complete
the mines, already having a luckstone, but I descended anyways. Wine
cellar - I carried a ton of potions to my stash for later
dilution/consumption. At some point, I found an amulet of reflection
down here, as well. Proceeded to use my first wish for +2 blessed grey
dragon scale mail. So, coming out of the mines, I had four of five
major pieces to my ascension kit already, including reflection and
magic resistance, as well as a good deal of protection.

3) Sokoban....Already had a bag of holding, as well as an amulet of
reflection....but there's lots of food, and a ton of exp waiting
inside. Fairly quick completion of this branch for another bag of
holding.

4)No big room, never found Ludios. Ran items to my stash for a while,
trying to hit level 14 for the quest. Found a couple robes, about 40
food rations, ='s of SlowDigestion, conflict, free action, gauntlets of
power, and a helm of brilliance during this time. RNG was being very
nice to me. I went ahead and used a few wishes in anticipation of the
castle's extra wand. Somewhere, I found yet another magic lamp. I added
speed boots to my kit, and a couple of " o Life Saving. In addition,
during this time I was awarded Flametongue (is that the right name??
Firebrand??), Excalibur (not dipped), and Ogresmasher.

5) Quest - The quest was fairly easy, but contained the first of my
'mishaps'. I ate/tinned the plentiful giants, easily hitting 18/** str
here before reaching Lord Surtur. In his cavern, I approached him with
a lava pool between us, pounding him with Mojo from afar. The idea was
to get some free hits until he ported/moved around the pool.
Unfortunately, I somehow missed catching Mojo on the return, and it
dropped into the lava...BAH....Well, I had wand's of cold (will they
work?), and earth, but I also had some erodeproof boots of levitation.
That should do the trick, right??? I finished off Surtur with
Flametongue (whatever) , jumped in the lava, and grabbed Mojo. Wasting
no time, I donned my boots to lift me out of the lava...ummm, lift
damnit.....uh oh....I was 'stuck'....A few monsters/turns later, one
amulet of life saving down. I will definitely not forget that little
mishap again....Lava....bad....

6) Medusa - A joke....Maybe 2 hits?? Mojo and a towel took care of her
fairly easy, and Perseus' statue contained the shield of reflection,
allowing me to wear my amulet full time (until later I used some wishes
to switch to silver dragon scale mail, cloak of MR, and #twoweapons).
Things were going fairly smooth, barring the one lava mishap...too
smooth...

7) Maze levels before Gehennom - At this point, I had most everything
for my kit, not highly enchanted, but all erodeproof at least. I also
had magic markers, scrolls, about 50 (no exaggeration) wands, tons of
rings, and all the other regular stuff (tinning kit, lock pick, lamp,
towel, unicorn horn, etc) Things were going great....And to make it
even better, here come 2 lovely nurses to tend to my 'wounds'. I'll
just disrobe and let them have their way......Ahhh, that feels great
ladies, just a little l- what!!! - no....NO!!!!.....During my
indiscretion with the nurses, something chose this as an opportune time
to attack, while I was naked and weaponless. I was paralyzed, blind,
and my HP's were going down. I didn't even have a single turn to apply
the horn, or wield Mojo. 2 amulets of life saving down.....

8) Gehennom....Well, 2 deaths under my belt, both avoidable, but not
avoided. TIme to be more careful. Several hours were spent moving up
and down the dungeon, collecting loot, bumping my hp's with potions,
stockpiling food, scrolls, and wands. Remembering the other time I had
gotten this far, and my 2 deaths this game already, I began to be much
more careful. Through luck, and a couple wishes, I ended up with 4 more
amulets of life saving. Vlad died quickly, and easily. Now I had the
bell and the candelabra. The final battle would soon be at hand. I was
farther than I had ever been before.

9) Orcus town - I used up a lot of my blank scrolls, and magic markers
to enchant my armor up a bit. An encounter with a few disenchanters had
left me weakened. All that was left at this point was to find the
square and the tower. So I dug down as deep as I could, and found the
square, actually very easily. Next, I started my way back up, exploring
and digging out the mazes in anticipation of my escape. Until finally,
I popped up in Orcus town, which would be the scene of my worst
encounter the whole game (well, that didn't end in a stupid death).
COming up the stairs, I spotted Orcus, shooting his wand of death
willy-nilly. Can't have that, I want that wand. I rushed him, hoping to
kill him before he used it up. Three steps from the stairs, his buddy,
the big Y, Yeenoghu, decides to join the party. Oh crap....2 named on
me now. Y summons a buttload of creatures around me, including 2
disenchanters in the adjacent spaces. Things went VERY poorly, and I
was losing about 50 hps a round. I actually managed to kill the horde,
at around 50ish hp's left (out of over 300, yikes). Somehow I killed
Orcus, but not before his wand of death exploded....dang.....My unicorn
horn was now cursed, and I had a close call when I applied it, trying
to cure blindness from a summoned raven, which promptly sickened me,
and made me halluciante. Yeenoghu died shortly after. However, I was in
VERY bad shape at this point. About half of my armor was cursed, my
horn was cursed, lots of my equipment was used up. I decided to trek
all the way back up to level 1 to my stash and rekit. I used a ton of
holy water repairing my armor, as well as my last wishes on a silver
saber, wand of death, and another marker. Also, I switched my GDSM and
shield of reflection for silver DSM and a cloak of MR. Also, I was
crowned at this time. This would be the last time I went to my stash
before the final run.


10) The tower...I wasn't sure what exactly what to expect here, having
never gotten this far before. I worked my way in, killed the wiz, and
grabbed the book of the dead.  The book dropped in the moat, but i used
a scroll of earth to fill it in and retrieve it. Nothing too bad
happened during the tower section, and I headed down for the final run.



11) Final run - Performing the invocation, I entered Moloch's sanctum.
A straight up fight ensued, and I slew a large number of creatures, but
was honestly never in any real danger. Even the high priest died fairly
easily, dropping 4 books in addition to the amulet. (Is it normal for
him to drop so many?) I had a moment to breathe, so, why not read the
spellbooks the priest dropped?? After all, I had a unicorn horn, money
wasn't an issue, and my bag was filled with tons of potions to fix
anything that happened from a cursed spell book. Except
paralysis.....bah.....the wizard beat me down for my last death, while
I was paralyzed. Dumb....But, you live and you learn....well, if you
have an amulet of life saving that is.


12) Run, Forrest....I was pulled down a few times in my dash to the
surface, and killed the wiz 3 or 4 times. But no big troubles. I
finally reached level one and my stash. Grabbed a huge bag of gems I
was saving, and double checked all my equipment. It was finally time. I
had never been to the planes before. I climbed the stairs....the air
twisted and distorted.....


13) I was finally in the planes....And I had no intention of
fighting....

  Earth>  I had 6 wands of digging ready....Read a ?o Gold Detection
while confused, and spotted the portal. Then proceeded to dig straight
there, only stopping to fight when forced. Earth was over quickly...

  Air> Same thing, spotted the portal, and, using =oLevitation, made a
beeline. FOught very little on this level. Piece of cake.

  Fire> Same tactic, of course. However, the lava worked to my
advantage this time. Leaving on the ring of levitation, I used the lava
as roadways, as a lot of the beasties couldn't follow me over it. Some
could - notably elementals - but not enough to stop me.

  Water> Water was slightly more difficult, but I didn't change my
tactics. The water forced me to move and fight in ways I didnt plan,
but I still ran straight for the portal.

The planes behind me, I prepared for the final level.


14) Astral Plane - I remembered reading that wearing conflict entering
the final plane was bad, as otherwise you would receive an angel pet.
Whcih I did. Unfortunately, no one told me that donning the =of
conflict AFTER receiving the angel would piss it off permanently. So I
had to kill my pet....bah....


I got lucky....I chose the right direction to go in, and only faced a
single rider, Famine, which wasn't too hard (to be honest, i don't even
remember killing him). I didn't even fight anyone inside the temple, I
simply ran to the altar and ascended....





This was a sloppy ascension, marred by poor planning, inexperience, and
not paying attention. (one note of interest, I had lost my quest
artifact somewhere on the planes) I probably would have been more
careful if I didn't have the 6 or 7 amulets of life saving. I KNOW I
would have changed my tactics had I only received a single one during
the game.


But it was a totally legit, no less sweet victory for having died 3
times!!! I finally did it!! Next time, I will be better prepared,
having at least faced the game from start to finish one time in it's
entirety.


